 *
 * COMPONENT TRIPLE
 * - Reason to exist : Axiom 9 architected — phase advancement is LEDGER AUDIT, not self-report.
 *                     Every predicate here is a mechanical check (§4.2.8): table lookup / regex /
 *                     count / fs stat over the W2 event ledger — no LLM call, read-only,
 *                     deterministic, statically bounded. The cheap layer decides everything it
 *                     CAN decide so the expensive layers only see what it cannot (§4.2.3).
 * - Axiom binding   : Axiom 9 (push architected), Axiom 1/2 via the mechanical-predicate
 *                     clause (§4.2.8, GAP-055 condition ①): these predicates check ACTIONS,
 *                     never reasoning — checking an action at a tool-call boundary is not an
 *                     intrusion into the reasoning window.
 * - Deprecation     : the predicate FAMILY is not deprecable (it is the gate's L1). Individual
 *                     floors follow §4.2.6: intensive invariants are mode-resident statics;
 *                     extensive floors are provisional until calibrated on the golden case set
 *                     (GAP-058) and MUST NOT produce FAIL-KILL while provisional.
 *
 * MECHANICAL PREDICATE CONTRACT (§4.2.8, decidable form):
 *   1. no model call   — this module imports ONLY node:fs / node:path and the W2 ledger reader;
 *                        the k3-stage-gate test walks the import graph from here and fails on
 *                        any provider/LLM module (GAP-055 condition ②).
 *   2. read-only       — predicates never mutate the judged object (writing the ledger happens
 *                        in stage-gate.ts AFTER judgment; the ledger is not the judged object).
 *   3. deterministic   — same input, same output; no randomness, no clock dependence.
 *   4. bounded         — single pass over the ledger / stat calls; no recursion, no retries.
 */

